\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Continuum multivectors and the rotation connection}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{The revised arXiv version of \citef{lasenby1998gravity},
Section 3.2, equation (3.21), p. 20, transforms continuum
multivectors by a rotor on the left and its reverse on the right.
Equations (3.26) and (3.28)–(3.31), pp. 20–21, introduce the
rotation connection and its derivative covariance. These locators
refer to gr-qc/0405033v1, the corrected revision of the 1998 article.}

\p{The finite [exterior rotational action](fdip-00YI) applies
the already defined vector action to each exterior factor. Its
pairing and transport covariance were proved in
\ref{fdip-00YK} and \ref{fdip-00YQ}. The cited continuum
connection does not supply those finite proofs or identify the
internal exterior factor with the cubical factor.}
